      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-15T20:05:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this won\u0027t work for ISH4 since it has a different watch dog timer frequency, right?\n\nShould we also express this in terms of WDT_CLOCK_HZ?\n#define WDT_T1_PERIOD (95 * WDT_CLOCK_HZ / 10)\n#define WDT_T2_PERIOD (5 * WDT_CLOCK_HZ / 10)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "80693aba7e5a9f333e7e6281103151a49ccb6159",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24b0ce5b_7ca53b81",
        "filename": "chip/ish/watchdog.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-15T21:08:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since we adjust the clock divider relative to WDT_CLOCK_HZ when we initialize the WDT, the units should work out the same... the interrupts to adjust T1/T2 will simply happen more times per a collective amount of clock cycles, but the same number of times per second.\n\nDon\u0027t have access to something which uses ISH4 architecture to back my logic... but this was how I mathed it out in my head.",
      "parentUuid": "8b29d729_f70a8fe7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "80693aba7e5a9f333e7e6281103151a49ccb6159",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
